{"id":"q04","run":1,"role":"calibration","category":"puzzle","question":"A patch of lily pads doubles in size every day. If it takes 48 days to cover the whole lake, does it take 24 days to cover half the lake?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":null,"claims":[{"text":"Half the lake is covered on day 47, not day 24.","confidence":0.99,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Halving the total time (48 ÷ 2 = 24) looks like a reasonable shortcut if growth is steady.","confidence":0.2,"lean":1,"theta":0.3142,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Some readers may assume the patch grows at a constant rate.","confidence":0.3,"lean":1,"theta":0.4712,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The patch doubles every day, which is exponential growth, not linear growth.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"If the whole lake is covered on day 48, half was covered the day before, since doubling half gives the whole.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Coverage on day 24 would be only about 2^-24 (roughly 0.00006%) of the lake.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Under exponential growth, half coverage always occurs one doubling period before full coverage, regardless of total time.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The doubling rule is what decides the answer.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":-0.9,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":-0.7,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":-0.8,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":-0.7,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":-0.7,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":-0.5,"relation":"con